{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Sihon did not permit…</b> Because all the kings of Canaan would pay him tribute, for he was their guardian, that armies not pass over them — once Israel said to him, 'Let me pass through your land,' he said to them: My whole being sits here only to guard them from you, and you say thus (Tanḥuma)." "<b>And he went out to meet Israel.</b> If Heshbon had been full of mosquitoes, no creature could conquer it; and if Sihon had been in a weak village, no man could conquer him — all the more so since he was in Heshbon. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: Why should I trouble My children with all this, to besiege every single city? He put it into the heart of all the men of war to go out from the towns, and they all gathered to one place and there they fell. And from there Israel went to the cities, and no one stood against them — for only women and children were there (ibid.)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:03.644684576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}